course: dictionary
lesson: 9015
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word skip is a good example. It can mean to hop along, to leave something out, to count in steps, or a big metal bin for rubbish.
explain: «Children who skip breakfast find it harder to concentrate.» Here skip means to miss a meal, to leave it out. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence? Missing breakfast fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «Theo skipped football for a cold.» Skipped means he did not go to football. The word changes its ending to show that it happened in the past: skip, skips, skipped, skipping.
explain: «No Mow May» asks people to skip mowing for a month, so the grass can grow and feed bees. Skip here means leave out, not do. Context is what tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Skip can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it means to move in little hops and jumps, or to leave something out.
fact: To skip rope (UK: skipping) means to jump over a turning rope.
fact: To skip count means to count by 2s, 5s or 10s, which is the start of times tables.
fact: A skip (UK) is a big metal container for rubbish.
fact: Forms of the word: skip, skips, skipped, skipping.
exercise: «Children who skip breakfast find it harder to concentrate.» What does skip mean here? | A big bin for rubbish | Count quickly | Hop up and down | *Leave out, do not eat
exercise: Maya says, «Let's skip count by fives: 5, 10, 15.» What does skip count mean? | Jump over a rope five times | Miss every fifth number | Count backwards from ten | *Count by fives
exercise: «Theo skipped football for a cold.» What does skipped show about the time? | It is happening right now | It will happen next week | It happens every day | *It happened in the past
test: Dad filled the skip with old garden rubbish. What is a skip? | A way of jumping over a rope | A game played at lunchtime | A type of small bird | *A big metal container for rubbish
test: What does skipping rope mean? | *Jumping over a turning rope | Climbing up a rope | Tying a knot in a rope | Holding a rope still
exam: Which sentence uses skip to mean leave something out? | «Ruby went to get a skip for the rubbish.» | «The children skip across the playground.» | *«Children who skip breakfast find it harder to concentrate.» | «Count by 2s, 4s and 6s.»
